\fs36\b\cf2 Quiz Setup and Quiz Taking\b0\cf1\fs22\par
\fs18\cf2 CTA LMS \endash  Client Documentation\cf1\fs22\par
\par
\fs20\b\cf4 Status: Working \endash  70% passing score, unlimited attempts, no time limit; certificate only after evaluation\b0\cf1\fs22\par
\par
\fs28\b\cf2 1. Overview\b0\cf1\fs22\par
\par
Each course can have one multiple-choice quiz. Admins build the quiz questions on the course edit screen. Students take the quiz after finishing all the course modules. If they pass, they must complete the structured course evaluation. Only after the evaluation is submitted is the CE certificate generated.\par
\par
Approved quiz rules (fixed by product policy):\par
- Passing score: 70%\par
- Attempts: unlimited retakes until the student passes\par
- Time limit: none (no countdown timer, no forced time-based submission)\par
\par
Completion sequence:\par
1. Complete all required modules\par
2. Pass the final quiz (70%+)\par
3. Complete the course evaluation\par
4. THEN the CE certificate is generated and downloadable\par
\par
\fs28\b\cf2 2. How it works (step by step)\b0\cf1\fs22\par
\par
Setting up (admin):\par
1. On the course edit screen, open the Quiz panel.\par
2. Give the quiz a title and add questions. Each question has the question text, four answer options (A\endash D), the correct option, and an optional explanation.\par
3. Save the quiz.\par
4. Configure the shared evaluation form under CTA LMS then Course Evaluation (add/edit/remove rating, multiple choice, and open-text questions).\par
\par
Taking the quiz (student):\par
1. The student must be logged in, enrolled, and have completed 100% of the modules.\par
2. They open the Quiz page, which shows the number of questions, the 70% passing score, Time Limit: No limit, and Attempts: Unlimited.\par
3. They click Start, answer the questions, and submit. There is no countdown timer.\par
4. The system scores the quiz. After a pass, they see: "Complete the course evaluation to receive your certificate."\par
5. They complete the evaluation form. The certificate is not available yet.\par
6. After evaluation submit, the certificate is generated and the download screen appears.\par
\par
\fs28\b\cf2 3. Where to find it\b0\cf1\fs22\par
\par
- Admin quiz: CTA LMS then Courses, open a course, Quiz panel.\par
- Admin evaluation questions: CTA LMS then Course Evaluation.\par
- Student side: the Quiz page shortcode, reached by the "Take Quiz" button in the course player.\par
\par
\fs28\b\cf2 4. What you can configure\b0\cf1\fs22\par
\par
- Quiz title and multiple-choice questions\par
- Evaluation form questions (rating scale, multiple choice, open text), sections, required flag, order, and active/inactive status\par
\par
\fs28\b\cf2 5. Current limitations / missing parts\b0\cf1\fs22\par
\par
- Quiz passing score / attempts / time limit are fixed by policy (not editable in admin).\par
- Only multiple-choice (A\endash D) quiz questions are supported.\par
- Only one quiz per course is supported.\par
- The evaluation step is required before the certificate is issued.\par
